{"kind":"assert","text":"BO1 admission-data gap: carry the requirement in a new Rules version. Answer to e487714b, amending ruling 7a2beda6 item 6.\n\nThe gap is real. The install is judged in the Rules scope: application-install-identities stores requirements as { destination, archive } (device-application-rules.ts:116; application-install.ts:178) and application-stage-definitions sends the directory name, declarations, definition texts, needsArchive, definition, job, release, semantic digest and additions (application-install.ts:239-246). Nothing names the commons, receive fields cannot be value places, and a directory guard that cannot see the requirement must not pretend to.\n\nAdopted: rules@14 joins the cohort, derived from rules@10 (the unpublished family's rules version; @11 to @13 are the certified, hardened and evidence families and stay as they are). rules@14 changes two things and nothing else: the requirements slot holds { destination, archive, commons } for every install, archive or not, so a non-archive package that requires commons is admitted rather than refused as unsupported install proof; and application-stage-definitions sends needsCommons beside needsArchive. directory@22's has-commons guard reads needsCommons from that message and refuses commons-missing when it is true and the directory's commons ref is absent. The host pre-check for rooms with older pins stands as ruled. A host boolean is not native evidence; the requirement reaches the directory only through the Rules scope's send.\n\nCOMMONS_COHORT is therefore register@23, directory@22, membership@9, rules@14, commons@1, with destination@16 and inbox@1 kept. The catalog goes from 80 to 85; docs/kernel.md K1 lists the five. rules@10 keeps its historical meaning; no existing pin changes. Witness: install of a commons-requiring package into a directory@22 room whose commons ref is present (admitted) and absent (commons-missing), and of an ordinary package in both (admitted), under the full gate and the kernel-gate review.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}